# Narrator: the foundation's test hillside. A placeholder (docs/PLACEHOLDERS.md): the Vagrant tells the real tale, in his own
# voice, once the voice bibles are signed off. These lines follow the Narrator's rules (second person, present tense, one or
# two sentences, concrete senses, no game terms) and stay short.

~ enter:test_hillside
| A hill leans up into the dark, with a creek talking to itself down its western side. Halfway up, a cottage sits on a shelf of level ground with one window lit.
once

~ examine:test_cottage
| The door is shut and the window glows orange. Whoever is inside has gone very quiet.

~ examine:test_well
| A stone well with a bucket on a frayed rope. Something down there is humming, softly, to the tune of the creek.

~ examine:test_scarecrow
| A scarecrow on its pole, with a carved turnip for a head and a candle stub burning behind the eyes. The face is grinning. You are fairly sure it was not, a moment ago.
